## `spec` fields

A cloud role a namespace brings to Shoal, and which workflows and agents may use it (§7.1).

At run time Shoal exchanges a credential that starts from its own deployment for short-lived
credentials of the role, scoped to one step attempt and attributed to the run and its initiator.

These are the top-level fields of the CloudIdentity spec, the same as `spec:` in YAML. Nested objects are described in the
server's JSON Schema at `GET /v1/schemas` (also used by the UI builder for validation).

| Field | Type | | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | optional |  |
| `provider` | string | optional | Credential provider plugin (shoal.credentials): aws. Default: `aws`. |
| `trust` | one of `web_identity`, `ambient` | optional | web_identity: the role trusts Shoal's OIDC issuer and Shoal presents a per-step token. ambient: the role trusts the deployment's own cloud identity (IRSA, Pod Identity, instance role), with a per-identity ExternalId; the operator must enable it. Default: `web_identity`. |
| `aws` | object | optional |  |
| `config` | map | optional | Settings for other providers. |
| `allow` | object | optional |  |

